CM_ "CAN FD frames tunnel classic CAN messages as chunks: 4-byte header (16-bit inner id, subid, dlc) followed by dlc data bytes, zero-padded at the end. Chunk order is fixed per address. Within each chunk data: byte 0 checksum, byte 1 low nibble rolling counter (0-14).";
CM_ SG_ 171 StrgWhlAngRate "reads 0 while the wheel is held steady; a steady angle is echoed on bytes 30-31 (unused copy of StrgWhlAng)";
CM_ SG_ 137 LKACmd "frozen at 0 while LKACmdSts is 0, tracks steering angle at ~16 counts/deg while stock LKA is active; angle vs torque request and scale unverified";
CM_ SG_ 137 LKACmdChksm "CRC8 poly 0x1D, init 0x00, no reflection/xorout, over chunk data bytes 1-7 (LKACmdRC/LKACmdSts byte through byte 7)";
CM_ SG_ 137 LKATorqueCmd "14-bit gated LKA command field, active only, does not move the wheel in highway data. Same message family as MG5 FVCM_HSC2_FrP03 (11-bit LKAReqToq torque + 14-bit LKAReqToqPV checksum): width matches the PV, but it holds ~89% of frames and ignores the counter, so it is not a counter-inclusive PV either. Torque vs PV unresolved; needs a curvy/active LKA drive";
CM_ SG_ 318 DrvrSbltBuckled "complementary pair with DrvrSbltUnbuckled, both zero when ignition is off";
CM_ SG_ 319 WhlSpdFR "front/rear axle assignment unverified, left/right verified via turns";
CM_ SG_ 1019 DircnIndSwSts "stalk state, no direction; use TURN_SIGNALS for direction";
CM_ BO_ 1808 "GWM/EVCC/BMS addresses from OBDb MG-MG4 signalset, possibly only reachable via the OBD-II port.";
CM_ BO_ 1842 "0x732/0x733/0x734/0x756 answered the VIN query (22 F190) on bus 0; FVCM/RADAR naming assumed from the MG5 FW query config, other ECUs unidentified.";
VAL_ 137 LKACmdSts 0 "OFF" 4 "ACTIVE";
VAL_ 404 ShftLvrPos 1 "P" 2 "R" 4 "D";
VAL_ 474 AccSts 0 "OFF" 1 "STANDBY" 2 "ACTIVE" 4 "OVERRIDE";
VAL_ 1019 DircnIndSwSts 0 "OFF" 1 "TAP" 2 "LATCHED";
